# p_7c29 — p_m3n4 — Doggy daycare Mon–Fri; both work 9-to-5

Both Hana and Priya work 9:00–17:00 office jobs. The dog (a medium-sized breed) goes to a daycare facility from 8:00 to 17:00 on weekdays. The 18:00 walkthrough: the dog is home (picked up at 17:00), which is why the dog bowl is on the kitchen floor and the toy is in the living room. Priya's entry items indicate she is arriving. On weekdays 8:00–17:00, the dog is OUT_OF_HOUSE (at daycare), so the dog bowl is empty, the leash is not used, and the dog food bag is not opened. On weekends, the dog is home all day: bowl is filled, leash is used for walks, toy is in active use. What sets this apart: the dog_bowl is empty (or the dog_toy is in storage) on weekday midday, and the dog_leash is OUT_OF_HOUSE on weekend mornings. What would refute it: finding the dog_toy in active use (on the floor near the dog) at 12:00 on a Tuesday, or finding the dog_leash in the house at 8:30 on a Saturday.

